Surely, if you can't control your pet, that's an argument for you to learn 
better gameplay rather than changing the game? By your own admission you 
forgot to close the shop door behind you.

There are plenty of ways to handle an overly powerful pet, such as leaving 
it one level above or below, locking it in a room (unless it can teleport), 
using a wand or potion of sleep, or even just keeping it interested with a 
supply of food elsewhere on the level (minetown guards are useful for 
this). Did you consider blocking those other entrances to the temple with 
cursed objects, or digging a row of pits? Of course, all of these have 
disadvantages as well, but the game isn't supposed to be too easy.

